**Examining PCI callbacks**

I see the user is pointing out the wording around "from every PCI PM callback... reaches i915_pm_suspend." We're looking at PCI PM operations, including direct calls like .suspend, .poweroff, and possibly freeze. They seem to want to understand the full call chain leading to i915_pm_suspend, maybe even in reverse from those PCI callbacks. I’ll need to check the definitions and look at the i915_drm_suspend display call to clarify things.
